## 6. The launcher icon — original work

**The launcher icon is original work by this project, released under this
repository's licence (`LICENSE`, Apache-2.0), and contains no third-party or
vendor material.** Recorded 2026-09-16.

| | |
|---|---|
| What it is | A lens ring with a white glass at its centre and two broadcast waves opening to the upper right — "a camera you command over a radio link". |
| Author | The project maintainer (`xiaobaiwud12`), as a work made for this project. |
| Terms | The same licence as the rest of the repository. No separate terms and no attribution obligation to anyone, because nothing was taken. |
| Where the artefacts are | `app/android/app/src/main/res/`: `drawable/ic_launcher_foreground.xml`, `drawable/ic_launcher_background.xml`, `drawable/ic_launcher_monochrome.xml`, the four `mipmap-anydpi-v26|v33/ic_launcher{,_round}.xml` manifests and the ten legacy PNGs under `mipmap-{m,h,xh,xxh,xxx}dpi/`. |
| Checked by | `app/tool/verify_icon.dart`, which decodes the PNGs, asserts they are neither blank nor mutually identical, and re-derives the safe-zone arithmetic from the written vector. |

Every artefact is derived from a single set of geometry constants, so the mark
exists in exactly one place rather than being drawn again per density.

### What it deliberately is not

* **Not the YI / Xiaoyi logo, wordmark or trade dress.** No logo was traced,
  recoloured or approximated, and the mark is not a camera body — a body
  silhouette is a manufacturer's shape, and copying one is exactly the trade
  dress this project must avoid. It is three primitives: a ring, a disc and two
  arcs. The arc angles, stroke weights and offsets were chosen here, by rendering
  candidates and looking at them.
* **Not from the vendor's application.** Nothing from the decompiled official
  application or its extracted resources contributed anything; none of that
  material is in this repository, and the release pipeline that produced this
  tree drops it by rule rather than by care.
* **Not from an icon set.** No icon font, no Material Symbols, no third-party
  SVG. Drawing it was cheaper than adding a dependency to a project whose
  dependency licences are enumerated in §2.

### The name under the icon

The launcher label is a string resource with an English and a Chinese value
(`app/android/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml`, `values-zh/strings.xml`)
rather than a literal. Which one a phone shows is decided by the **system**
locale, through `PackageManager`, before any Dart code runs — so the in-app
language picker cannot influence it, and this repository says so rather than
implying otherwise.

